WEBVTT

NOTE
English captions for "Sentencing of Nazi Leaders at Nuremberg" (National Archives
Identifier 23769). The words are the International Military Tribunal's judgment, read
on 30 September and 1 October 1946, as the trial's record publishes it (the Avalon
Project, Yale Law School), checked against the soundtrack: where the record's two
printings differ, the one the soundtrack agrees with. Where the soundtrack carries the
Russian or French interpretation, the record's English is given, marked [In Russian]
or [In French]. An ellipsis marks speech cut by the film's editing.

1
00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:27.400
…1941, spoke in terms of
fifty or a hundred lives

2
00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:31.800
from the occupied areas of the Soviet
Union for one German life taken.

3
00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:36.090
The order stated that
“it should be remembered

4
00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:38.600
that a human life in unsettled countries

5
00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:44.400
frequently counts for nothing and a
deterrent effect can be obtained only by…

6
00:01:57.600 --> 00:02:01.300
[In Russian] …and their relatives informed
that they had died from natural causes.

7
00:02:01.900 --> 00:02:07.200
The victims were not confined to German
citizens, but included foreign laborers

8
00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:09.270
who were no longer able to work,

9
00:02:09.270 --> 00:02:12.700
and were therefore useless
to the German war machine.

10
00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:18.500
It has been estimated that… in
nursing homes, hospitals, and asylums…

11
00:02:18.500 --> 00:02:23.000
When the witness Von dem
Bach-Zelewski was asked

12
00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:27.700
how Ohlendorf could admit the
murder of 90,000 people, he replied:

13
00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:32.800
“I am of the opinion that
when for years, for decades,

14
00:02:32.800 --> 00:02:37.600
the doctrine is preached that the Slav…”

15
00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:42.600
“It is certainly no coincidence
that the fateful year 1938

16
00:02:42.600 --> 00:02:46.900
has brought nearer the
solution of the Jewish question

17
00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:50.800
simultaneously with the realization
of the idea of Greater Germany,

18
00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:53.600
since the Jewish policy was both the basis

19
00:02:53.600 --> 00:02:56.800
and consequence of the
events of the year 1938.

20
00:02:57.200 --> 00:03:01.100
The advance made by Jewish influence
and the destructive Jewish spirit

21
00:03:01.100 --> 00:03:04.000
in politics, economy, and culture
paralyzed the power and the will

22
00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:10.000
of the German people to rise
again, more perhaps even

23
00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:12.300
than the power policy opposition

24
00:03:12.300 --> 00:03:16.400
of the former enemy Allied
powers of the first World War.”

25
00:03:17.900 --> 00:03:23.000
…of the WVHA, they were used
as a source of slave labor.

26
00:03:24.800 --> 00:03:29.100
An agreement made with the Ministry
of Justice on 18 September 1942

27
00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:34.500
provided that antisocial elements
who had finished prison sentences

28
00:03:34.500 --> 00:03:38.400
were to be delivered to the
SS to be worked to death.

29
00:03:39.500 --> 00:03:45.700
Steps were continually taken, involving
the use of the Security Police and SD

30
00:03:45.700 --> 00:03:49.800
and even the Waffen-SS,
to insure that the SS had

31
00:03:49.800 --> 00:03:53.600
an adequate supply of concentration
camp labor for its projects.

32
00:03:55.500 --> 00:03:59.000
In connection with the administration
of the concentration camps,

33
00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:02.300
the SS embarked on a series
of experiments on human beings

34
00:04:02.300 --> 00:04:07.000
which were performed on prisoners of
war or concentration camp inmates.

35
00:04:07.100 --> 00:04:12.600
These experiments included freezing to
death and killing by poison bullets.

36
00:04:13.800 --> 00:04:18.900
The SS was able to obtain an allocation of
Government funds for this kind of research

37
00:04:18.900 --> 00:04:21.900
on the grounds that they had access

38
00:04:21.900 --> 00:04:25.900
to human material not
available to other agencies.

39
00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:32.000
The SS played a particularly significant
role in the persecution of the Jews.

40
00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:37.200
The SS was directly involved in the
demonstrations of 10 November 1938.

41
00:04:38.300 --> 00:04:41.300
The evacuation of the Jews
from occupied territories

42
00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:44.200
was carried out under
the directions of the SS

43
00:04:44.200 --> 00:04:46.900
with the assistance of SS Police units.

44
00:04:47.700 --> 00:04:49.900
The extermination of
the Jews was carried out

45
00:04:49.900 --> 00:04:52.100
under the direction of the
SS central organizations.

46
00:04:52.900 --> 00:04:55.400
It was actually put into
effect by SS formations.

47
00:04:58.600 --> 00:05:02.900
Where the facts warrant it, these
men should be brought to trial

48
00:05:02.900 --> 00:05:08.300
so that those among them who are guilty of
these crimes should not escape punishment.

49
00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:18.700
The Tribunal will sit
tomorrow at 9:30 A.M.,

50
00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:21.500
and the Tribunal will now adjourn.

51
00:05:23.900 --> 00:05:26.800
[A voice] Hello, sound recording.
Hello, sound recording.

52
00:05:27.400 --> 00:05:30.300
Adjourn till tomorrow at 9:30.

53
00:05:46.700 --> 00:05:51.200
…in 1933 and was charged
with consolidating this power

54
00:05:51.200 --> 00:05:54.400
and expanding German armed might.

55
00:05:55.400 --> 00:05:59.700
He developed the Gestapo and created
the first concentration camps,

56
00:06:00.900 --> 00:06:05.300
relinquishing them to Himmler in 1934,

57
00:06:05.300 --> 00:06:08.300
conducted the Roehm purge in that year,

58
00:06:08.300 --> 00:06:12.500
and engineered the sordid
proceedings which resulted

59
00:06:12.500 --> 00:06:16.900
in the removal of Von Blomberg
and Von Fritsch from the Army.

60
00:06:20.200 --> 00:06:24.400
…food surplus regions, a
diversion of food to German needs.

61
00:06:27.500 --> 00:06:31.000
Goering claims its purposes
have been misunderstood,

62
00:06:31.000 --> 00:06:34.600
but admits “that as a matter
of course and a matter of duty

63
00:06:34.700 --> 00:06:38.500
we would have used Russia for
our purposes” when conquered.

64
00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:45.300
And he participated in the
conference of 16th July, 1941,

65
00:06:45.300 --> 00:06:49.000
when Hitler said the National Socialists

66
00:06:49.000 --> 00:06:53.000
had no intention of ever
leaving the occupied countries,

67
00:06:53.000 --> 00:06:59.500
and that “all necessary measures—shooting,
desettling, etc.—” should be taken.

68
00:07:02.300 --> 00:07:07.500
[In Russian] There is no suggestion
that Hess was not completely sane

69
00:07:07.500 --> 00:07:12.800
when the acts charged
against him were committed.

70
00:07:13.500 --> 00:07:14.600
Conclusion:

71
00:07:14.600 --> 00:07:19.000
The Tribunal finds the Defendant
Hess guilty on Counts One and Two;

72
00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:25.200
and not guilty on Counts Three and Four.

73
00:07:41.200 --> 00:07:47.500
By 1933 he had been made foreign
policy adviser to Hitler,

74
00:07:48.500 --> 00:07:52.900
and in the same year the representative
of the Nazi Party on foreign policy.

75
00:07:54.300 --> 00:07:57.400
…he took part in a conference
between Hitler and Horthy

76
00:07:57.400 --> 00:08:00.400
on the deportation of Jews from Hungary

77
00:08:00.800 --> 00:08:04.300
and informed Horthy that
the “Jews must either

78
00:08:04.300 --> 00:08:08.900
be exterminated or taken
to concentration camps.”

79
00:08:09.500 --> 00:08:14.900
At the same conference Hitler had likened
the Jews to “tuberculosis bacilli”

80
00:08:14.900 --> 00:08:19.800
and said if they did not
work they were to be shot.

81
00:08:21.400 --> 00:08:24.600
Ribbentrop’s defense to the
charges made against him

82
00:08:24.600 --> 00:08:28.900
is that Hitler made all
the important decisions,

83
00:08:28.900 --> 00:08:33.600
and that he was such a great admirer
and faithful follower of Hitler

84
00:08:33.600 --> 00:08:39.600
that he never questioned Hitler’s
repeated assertions that he wanted peace

85
00:08:41.200 --> 00:08:46.000
or the truth of the reasons that Hitler
gave in explaining aggressive action.

86
00:08:48.200 --> 00:08:50.200
…was whole-hearted.

87
00:08:51.000 --> 00:08:55.400
It was because Hitler’s policy and
plans coincided with his own ideas

88
00:08:55.400 --> 00:09:01.000
that Ribbentrop served him
so willingly to the end.

89
00:09:02.100 --> 00:09:08.900
Conclusion: The Tribunal finds that
Ribbentrop is guilty on all four Counts.

90
00:09:17.400 --> 00:09:21.000
[In French] Superior
orders, even to a soldier,

91
00:09:21.000 --> 00:09:23.600
cannot be considered in mitigation

92
00:09:23.600 --> 00:09:26.400
where crimes so shocking and extensive

93
00:09:26.400 --> 00:09:29.800
have been committed
consciously, ruthlessly,

94
00:09:29.800 --> 00:09:32.600
and without military
excuse or justification.

95
00:09:32.600 --> 00:09:40.000
Conclusion: The Tribunal finds
Keitel guilty on all four Counts.

96
00:09:43.500 --> 00:09:44.900
Kaltenbrunner.

97
00:09:45.300 --> 00:09:49.000
Kaltenbrunner is indicted under
Counts One, Three, and Four.

98
00:09:50.100 --> 00:09:53.400
He joined the Austrian Nazi
Party and the SS in 1932.

99
00:09:55.200 --> 00:09:58.400
In 1935 he became leader
of the SS in Austria.

